@ 2 0 0 1f5d14de22d759d41ccada733bfdabe0
+ A change which applies throughout a document, such as renaming a keyword wherever it occurs, is
+ a `transform`. It applies a function to every compound, the deepest first, and keeps everything
+ which is not a compound exactly as it was: comments, blank lines, the pragma and the layout.
+
+ ```scala
+ val shouted = document.transform: compound =>
+   compound.copy(keyword = compound.keyword.upper)
+ ```
+
+ ```scala fuel
+ run
+ ##
+ Out.println(shouted.show)
+ ```
+
+ The tree which `transform` walks can also be read directly. A parsed value's `document` is its
+ `Tel.Document`, with the pragma and line endings it was read with, and its `blocks` are the
+ compounds as they are laid out: each `Tel.Block` holds the comments above a group of compounds,
+ the compounds themselves, and the number of blank lines after them.
+
+ ```scala fuel
+ run
+ ##
+ document.blocks.each: block =>
+   Out.println(t"${block.comments.length} ${block.compounds.length} ${block.trailingBlankLines}")
+ ```
+

